The cleanest: process all touching bricks but ensure only ONE velocity flip pair happens. I'll do: find all overlapping bricks, compute the net bounce. Since in a seam the two bricks have the same face normal, we want a single bounce. 

Approach: Iterate bricks; for the first overlapping brick, apply bounce (flip + push out). Then for subsequent bricks, since the ball has been pushed out, check again — if it no longer overlaps, skip; if it still overlaps (different axis, e.g. corner of 4 bricks), we need to resolve that too but without cancelling.

